{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg7xZNSm7U3qtRfhgYNaE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I fixed two bugs in `cache/lru.py`, and the tests pass (2 passed).\n\n- **`get`:** it now marks the key as most recently used. Before, reading an entry didn't protect it from eviction.\n- **`put`:** updating an existing key now also marks it as most recently used, and it no longer evicts anything. Before, a full cache evicted the oldest entry even when you were only updating a key already in it. It now evicts only when you add a new key.\n\nThe public API is unchanged."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 639, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2385, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 639}, "output_tokens": 160, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ec5cbc41-398a-4947-8b28-c51ca0d1e1ff", "uuid": "56450a6b-a813-41c8-a312-07c036d4b1cf", "timestamp": "2026-10-17T14:22:04.867Z", "request_id": "req_011Cg7xZNBstkvN8RdAPc5yw"}
